 ## Overview
-This method computes the forward projection of a volume defined by box splines and its analytical gradients with respect to ray parameters (origin $\mathbf{t}$ and direction $\mathbf{n}$) and volume data coefficients. It implements the differentiable X-ray transform operator, supporting 2D and 3D uniform grids with interpolation orders 0, 1, and 2. Unlike standard differentiable renderers that rely on finite differences or implicit automatic differentiation through the entire ray march, this method explicitly computes ray-traced geometry gradients for anchors and directions using specific adjoint functions, while using the standard adjoint transform for volume coefficients. It is primarily used in geometry calibration in tomography.
+This method computes the forward projection of a volume defined by box splines and its analytical gradients with respect to ray parameters (origin $t$ and direction $n$) and volume data coefficients [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of differentiable X-ray transform (XRT) for uniform grids, supporting 2D and 3D domains with interpolation orders 0, 1, and 2 [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard differentiable renderers that rely on finite differences or implicit automatic differentiation through the entire ray-marching loop, this method explicitly computes ray-traced geometry gradients using specific adjoint functions for ray anchors and directions, while using the standard adjoint transform for volume coefficients [S1, unofficial]. It is primarily used in geometry calibration for tomography [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-The method computes the projection integral $\int_{\mathbb{R}} f(\mathbf{t} + \tau \mathbf{n}) d\tau$ for a volume $f(\mathbf{x}) = \sum_{\mathbf{q}} f_{\mathbf{q}} \psi(\mathbf{x} - \mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{q}})$, where $\psi$ is a box spline basis function determined by the interpolation order. The volume is defined on a uniform grid with start $\mathbf{x}_0$, step $\mathbf{\Delta}$, and dimensions $\mathbf{Q}$.
+The method implements the differentiable X-ray transform operator $\mathcal{X}[f](\mathbf{n}, \mathbf{t}) = \int_{\mathbb{R}} f(\mathbf{t} + \tau \mathbf{n}) d\tau$ for a volume $f(\mathbf{x}) = \sum_{\mathbf{q} \in \text{discreteRange}(\mathbf{0}, \mathbf{Q}-1)} f_{\mathbf{q}} \psi(\mathbf{x} - \mathbf{x}_{\mathbf{q}})$, where $\psi$ is a box spline basis function determined by the interpolation order [S1, unofficial]. The volume is defined on a uniform grid with start $\mathbf{x}_0$, step $\mathbf{\Delta}$, and dimensions $\mathbf{Q}$ [S1, unofficial].
 
